Prepare a blank by 
using the sample, after having first oxidized the hydrazine in the sample by suitable means, 
in the case of highlycolored water.Determine the completeness of the oxidation of the hydrazine by making a plot of the percentage transmittance ( compared to water to which the reagents have been added ) versus wavelength for the spectral region 400 to500 nm, and nothing whether the characteristic dip of pdimethylaminobenzalazine occurs at 458 nm.

